Change-ID: CL-20260803-121
Commit: pending
Date: 2026-08-03
Type: Fix -- the atom registry fills for the first time
Request-or-TODO: Process-refinement analysis item 5
Outcome: Every run of this session recorded "0 of N produced atom(s) carried
  schema-v1 //codeflux:atom documentation". Deriving the documentation from
  measured facts was the right half of the answer and it still registered
  nothing, for two reasons neither of which was visible.
  The schema block was inserted above StartLine, which points at the doc
  comment rather than at the declaration, so it landed before the ordinary
  comment and the prose that followed read as a continuation of the last field.
  It now goes directly above the func keyword, which is where the schema's own
  instruction has always said to put it.
  Seven of the nineteen fields are lists, read from lines beginning with a
  dash, and they were written as prose. The document was refused with 'field
  "Inputs" is empty' against a line reading "int, []int" -- a field that
  visibly has words in it. Those seven now emit items.
  Neither reason was reachable from any record. Registration counted refusals
  and discarded why, so "0 of 2 produced atoms" was the whole account. The
  reasons are now carried in the stage's evidence, traced per atom, and named
  in the stage detail, which is what made both defects findable in one run
  instead of one per guess.
Verification: Build, vet, gofmt, and a new test that drives an undocumented
  atom through derivation into the registry and reads the revision back out of
