Change-ID: CL-20260803-118
Commit: pending
Date: 2026-08-03
Type: Fix -- a run may not return with its task still running
Request-or-TODO: Terminal-state analysis of the rung 3 run, 2026-08-03
Outcome: The stall was never the circuit breaker. completeRunIfPossible had
  fifteen bare returns in it, every one a real decision -- the evidence did not
  resolve, a required stage did not hold, the revision could not be read -- and
  every one left the task in `running` with nothing recorded. The ladder waited
  for a terminal state nothing was going to write. Rung 3 verified its work at
  60 seconds, finished its checks at 71, and sat there until the enclosing
  timeout.
  Completion now returns a finalization carrying whether the ending is terminal
  and why. A caller that gets a non-terminal result gives the run an ending
  itself, conditional on the task still being running so a specific outcome
  already recorded is never overwritten by this generic one.
  Path coverage, atom documentation, and both registration stages are declared
  advisory. They are refinement-ceiling gates: a coverage percentage below a
  threshold and an atom without a registry row are both real and neither makes
  the program wrong. The completion floor -- assembly, integration tests,
  end-to-end, atom verification -- can never be advisory, and a test says so,
  because a program that does not build must never read as awaiting review.
  The terminal record moved after the transition it describes. It used to be
  written before, which made it a prediction: it named a status while the task
  was still running, and the two could disagree with nobody the wiser.
  The atom schema is now derived from what the run measured rather than asked
  of the model. All nineteen fields are facts the analysis already holds -- the
  signature gives inputs and outputs, the effect analysis gives effects and
  determinism, ReturnsError gives failure semantics, LoopDepth gives the
  complexity bound. It runs after verification, against the verified tree, and
  is reverted whole if it breaks anything: a registry row is worth having and
  is not worth a working program.
Verification: Build, vet, gofmt, three new finalization tests
