Change-ID: CL-20260803-116
Commit: pending
Date: 2026-08-03
Type: Fix -- a run that has converged is allowed to finish
Request-or-TODO: Trace analysis of the rung 3 run, 2026-08-03
Outcome: The implementation loop had converged; the orchestration loop had not.
  Rung 3 captured three verified checkpoints inside 135 seconds and then spent
  272 more seconds waiting out identical provider failures without touching the
  worktree. It possessed a verified result and treated unavailable refinement
  capacity as a reason not to finish.
  A circuit breaker now closes that. Two identical infrastructure failures --
  same category, same tree hash -- against an existing verified checkpoint end
  refinement and finalise from the checkpoint. A different category or a
  changed tree resets the count, because either means something happened
  between the failures.
  Findings are fingerprinted with their identifiers removed, so "main calls
  run, which can fail" and "main calls runCommand, which can fail" are one
  criticism rather than two. The callee is dropped by position rather than by
  shape: "run" is a name in that sentence and a common verb everywhere else,
  and nothing about the word itself tells them apart.
  Completion and refinement are now separate thresholds. A measured defect --
  one the tests were actually run against and did not catch -- still blocks. A
  mechanical rule's opinion, once attempted and raised again, is carried as an
  advisory and the run finishes.
  Every exit path emits a terminal record: the status, the verified revision
  and why it was verified, whether the worktree is that revision, attempts
  split between productive and lost-to-the-provider, unresolved work, and the
  advisories carried rather than fixed.
  The adversarial instruction stopped claiming the tests were unproven. It read
  the narrator's flags and told the model its tests "have not been shown to
  pass" in the same run whose trace says a checkpoint was captured because they
  had; the suite is re-run on that exact tree a few lines earlier, so the fact
  is known rather than inferred.
