  read-time hazard rather than the numbering: a stage's classification is
  re-derived from its persisted number against the running binary's tables,
  including for every row of every historical ledger the frontend renders. A
  renumber would leave old rows' names correct and their reasons describing a
  different stage, with nothing to notice the disagreement
Affected-behavior: None yet. Nothing consults a profile
Compatibility-or-migration: decline.go is extended additively; the existing
  classification path is unchanged
Verification: The discriminating test drives the real scheduler rather than a
  model of it -- RestrictToStages and RunConcurrently, once per profile -- and
  proves the runner is never invoked at all for a declined stage
Known-limitations: Zero production call sites. Every place stage selection or
  classification happens is in a file this change does not own, so the profile
  is declared and not yet consulted; that is stated in the plan section this
  ticket adds rather than left for a reader to discover. Filed as PIPE-046a.
  PIPE-045 needs decline classification rekeyed by stage name, migration 31's
  1-to-64 bound widened, and a rows-copy migration that respects the
  append-only trigger rather than defeating it. Filed as PIPE-045a
