  had piped stdin through the mediated boundary and acceptance examples and
  hostile probes need it. Public stage signatures are unchanged
Verification: Three discriminating tests, one per call site, each passing under
  mediation and failing without it. The abuse case runs repository test code
  attempting all three escapes at once and reruns the identical fixture
  unmediated: the credential payload is empty under mediation and carries the
  real key without it
Known-limitations: PIPE-132 and PIPE-133 are partial and stay open. Network
  reach and writes outside the worktree are not refused; the abuse case logs
  both as observed rather than asserting a containment that does not exist.
  Filed as PIPE-132a and PIPE-133a.
  Cost measured rather than estimated: ResolveExecutableIdentity hashes the
  whole go.exe on every mediated call, 107ms isolated against 34us for LookPath,
  giving 4.25s to 4.82s over eight calls in the mutation stage. It was left
  alone because it is shared by every mediated command repository-wide
