Date: 2026-08-02
Type: Change -- share the shell-out, not the tree
Request-or-TODO: PIPE-057
Outcome: The ticket asked to stop re-parsing produced source about twenty times
  a run. Measurement says the parse is not the cost: parseProducedFunctions runs
  in 0-506 microseconds, while producedGoFiles is a git status process spawn at
  18-22ms. Six of each is roughly 120ms of a 3.8s run.
  So the cache memoizes the file list, the parsed tree, tested names and
  documented names for the four checks examineStructure runs consecutively, and
  the four shell-outs collapse to one. It also removes a fully wasted parse:
  resolveAttribution built an attributedScope that both of its callers discarded
Affected-behavior: None. No check's verdict changes
Compatibility-or-migration: None
Verification: The cache is keyed on the exact sorted file list, never on the
  worktree, so an attribution-derived list and a git-status-derived list cannot
  share an entry -- a conflation that would be a correctness bug, and there is a
  test for it. Each test proven to discriminate by injecting the exact defect
Known-limitations: Wall clock is noise-dominated and is reported as such rather
  than dressed up: five lanes were editing this checkout, a controlled A/B
  drifted together as load rose, and the provable saving is below the noise
  floor. The structural claim is guaranteed by the code, not sampled.
  checkSimplification is deliberately uncached because it runs after mutation
  testing writes and restores files in place
