Change-ID: CL-20260802-055
Commit: da61102
Date: 2026-08-02
Type: Agent worktrees are prohibited; everyone works in the dev checkout
Request-or-TODO: User: "lets never use worktrees, just tell the agents to build
  inside of dev and be careful to not clobber other agents changes"
Outcome: AGENTS.md's "One Lane, One Worktree" is replaced by "Everyone Works in
  dev, Nobody Clobbers". Agents no longer create a worktree or a second clone;
  they work directly in the dev checkout alongside each other, and the
  co-tenancy rules become the discipline instead of the workaround: stage
  explicit paths and never git add -A; stage only your own hunk when a shared
  file carries another lane's work; re-read CHANGELOG and DEVLOG immediately
  before writing an entry because identifiers move and have already collided;
  never revert, reformat, or repair a file you did not change, the one exception
  being a mechanical gofmt left unstaged; expect a syntactically broken tree that
  is not yours and wait rather than fixing it; never rewrite shared history; and
  treat the fixed-port dev server as shared. The section states the accepted cost
  plainly -- a repository-wide gate can be red for reasons unrelated to you, and
  a push carries whatever else is unpushed -- and that this is not a licence to
  route around a gate. The prohibition is explicitly scoped to agent working
  copies; the per-task worktrees the product creates in internal/gitwork are
  untouched, and the section says so, because a later agent reading only the
  heading could otherwise remove a product feature
Affected-behavior: None at runtime
Compatibility-or-migration: Supersedes CL-20260802-022. Any worktree created
  under the previous rule should be removed with git worktree remove
Verification: Prose only; no Go source touched
Dev-Log: DL-20260802-065

